{"id":"n-20261006-gm2lr0","category":"tech","display_title":"Nintendo Switch Sports Resort","display_title_he":"נינטנדו סוויץ' ספורטס ריזורט","short_summary":"Nintendo is set to release Nintendo Switch Sports Resort exclusively for the Switch 2 on October 22, combining motion-controlled sports with nostalgic nods to classic titles.","english_level":"C1","words":406,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Nintendo_Switch_game_card_-_1.jpg/960px-Nintendo_Switch_game_card_-_1.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Kyu3a · CC BY-SA 4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nintendo_Switch_game_card_-_1.jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"Polygon","domain":"polygon.com","url":"https://www.polygon.com/nintendo-switch-sports-resort-preview-switch-2","title":"Nintendo's New Switch Sports Is the Best of Wii Sports, Wave Race, and More","published_at":"2026-10-06T13:01:16.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-06T13:01:16.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-06T15:17:26.642Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Back in 2006, Nintendo introduced motion-controlled gaming to a global audience with Wii Sports, a remarkably newcomer-friendly release that achieved massive commercial success by selling 82 million copies. Following several sequels across various consoles, Nintendo is now preparing to launch Nintendo Switch Sports Resort, an exclusive title for the upcoming Nintendo Switch 2. According to hands-on reports from a recent one-hour preview, this upcoming installment stands as the most comprehensive collection of motion-controlled sports games in the franchise thus far, blending casual pick-up-and-play mechanics with clear tributes to the company's treasured classic catalog. Scheduled for release on October 22, the game incorporates returning favorites alongside fresh experiences that recall older franchises such as Wave Race, Pilotwings, and Punch-Out!!, and potentially even Tony Hawk's Pro Skater.","Among the returning activities are updated iterations of bowling, golf, and tennis. The new version of bowling features one hundred-pin gameplay, while split-screen table tennis provides a frantic alternative to traditional tennis matches. Furthermore, the increased precision of the new Joy-Con 2 motion controls makes these activities feel more responsive than ever before. Beyond traditional sports, the software introduces a skateboarding activity that allows players to cruise across the resort-style getaway of Wuhu Island, collecting tokens and discovering photo-op locations within a relaxed, cooperative sightseeing mode that features an unpressured timer. The control scheme utilizes the right controller turned on its side, enabling users to pull back for acceleration, tilt left and right for steering, and lift upward to execute jumps and tricks.","Additional modes include Power Cruising and Prop Plane, which offer experiences reminiscent of Wave Race and Pilotwings. Power Cruising places players on a personal watercraft steered by holding both controllers in front like handlebars, letting users jump over ramps and collect tokens around Wuhu Island. Meanwhile, Prop Plane delivers a tranquil glider experience where users hold a single controller like a paper airplane, flying through rings and shooting down balloons across the island. Meanwhile, more competitive offerings feature Archery, where four participants shoot at a shared target and aim for specific quadrants while trying to steal points from opponents, alongside a revised boxing mode that matches players against CPU opponents in a one-on-one bout. Although activities like Thumb Wrestling appear less essential due to pinning massive digital thumbs in a show of dominance, the overall package provides a diverse array of cooperative and competitive options designed to appeal to various types of players when it arrives on the Switch 2 system later this month."],"facts":[{"fact":"Nintendo announced Nintendo Switch Sports Resort, a Switch 2 exclusive scheduled for release on October 22.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The game is the most comprehensive motion-controlled sports collection in the series, featuring activities like bowling, tennis, golf, skateboarding, power cruising, prop plane, thumb wrestling, archery, and boxing.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The title utilizes updated Joy-Con 2 motion controls to offer improved fidelity and gameplay reminiscent of classic titles like Wii Sports, Wave Race, Pilotwings, Punch-Out!!, and Tony Hawk's Pro Skater.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"back in","lemma":"back in","pos":"prepositional phrase","he":"בחזרה ב־ / בשנת","name":false},{"text":"2006","lemma":"2006","pos":"number","he":"2006","name":"2006"},{"text":"Nintendo","lemma":"Nintendo","pos":"proper noun","he":"נינטנדו","name":"Nintendo"},{"text":"introduced","lemma":"introduce","pos":"verb","he":"הציג","name":false},{"text":"motion-controlled","lemma":"motion-controlled","pos":"adjective","he":"נשלט תנועה","name":false},{"text":"gaming","lemma":"gaming","pos":"noun","he":"גיימינג / משחקי מחשב","name":false},{"text":"global","lemma":"global","pos":"adjective","he":"עולמי","name":false},{"text":"audience","lemma":"audience","pos":"noun","he":"קהל","name":false},{"text":"Wii Sports","lemma":"Wii Sports","pos":"proper noun","he":"ווי ספורט","name":"Wii Sports"},{"text":"remarkably","lemma":"remarkably","pos":"adverb","he":"באופן יוצא דופן","name":false},{"text":"newcomer-friendly","lemma":"newcomer-friendly","pos":"adjective","he":"ידידותי למתחילים","name":false},{"text":"release","lemma":"release","pos":"noun","he":"השקה / משחק","name":false},{"text":"achieved","lemma":"achieve","pos":"verb","he":"השיג","name":false},{"text":"massive","lemma":"massive","pos":"adjective","he":"עצום","name":false},{"text":"commercial","lemma":"commercial","pos":"adjective","he":"מסחרי","nam